{
  "description": "Deterministic retrieval + pipeline eval. No LLM call, no cost — meant to run on every change (architecture doc §6.7). Case types: standard (answer exists, must be found), acl_test (access control), and refusal (answer does NOT exist in the corpus and the system must say so rather than return a confident near-miss).",
  "notes": {
    "refusal_cases": "These calibrate ABSOLUTE_RELEVANCE_FLOOR. Without them the floor was tuned on 4 hand-picked examples, which is not enough to distinguish 'correctly refused' from 'broken and refusing everything'. A floor set too high fails these; a floor set too low fails them by inventing answers.",
    "keyword_matching": "expected_keywords are checked case-insensitively against concatenated retrieved chunk text."
  },
  "cases": [
    {
      "id": "vacation-days",
      "question": "How many vacation days do full-time employees get per year?",
      "user_groups": ["public"],
      "expected_document_contains": "Employee Handbook",
      "expected_keywords": ["18", "vacation"],
      "top_k": 5
    },
    {
      "id": "vacation-rollover",
      "question": "How many unused vacation days can roll over to next year?",
      "user_groups": ["public"],
